  "id": "listening-attitude",
  "term": "listening attitude",
  "definition": "In this historical usage, a listening attitude is a person’s sudden manner of pausing and seeming to attend to an unheard speaker. It was described as a sign that could suggest hearing voices, especially if the person then whispered or called back in reply.",
